@CC ===================================================================
@CC (SYSTEM)LOAD-MODE:MODE   --- GENERIC TEMPLATE (warm-start config) ---
@CC The real warm-start content. Called from LOAD-MODE:BATC (batch), or
@CC run by hand:  @MODE (SYSTEM)LOAD-MODE:MODE,,,
@CC No @ENTER and no password here -- it runs in the caller's context.
@CC Replace the <TOKEN>s; delete OPTIONAL lines you do not use.
@CC ===================================================================
@SET-UNAVAILABLE $THE COMPUTER IS BEING STARTED$
@CC
@CC --- Directories & floppy drives (main dir entered by INITIAL-COMMAND)
@DEFINE-MASS-STORAGE-UNIT FLOPPY-DISC-1 0
@CC @ENTER-DIRECTORY <OTHER-DIR> <DISC-DEVICE> <UNIT>
@CC @SET-DEFAULT-DIRECTORY <OTHER-DIR>
@CC
@CC --- Terminal types (OPTIONAL; one line per terminal, site-specific)-
@CC @SET-TERMINAL-TYPE <term-no> <type>
@CC
@CC --- Extra batch processors (only if you use batch 2+, else leave off)
@CC @BATCH 2
@CC
@CC --- Start XMSG and bring up the network links ----------------------
@MODE (SYSTEM)XMSG-START:MODE,,,
@CC
@CC --- Start COSMOS Basic Module (OPTIONAL; needs XMSG up) ------------
@CC     Starts TADADM internally via the file-server part.
@MODE (<COSMOS-USER>)COS-START-<REV>:MODE,,
@CC
@CC --- If you did NOT install the COSMOS file-server part, uncomment: --
@CC @START-TADADM
@CC
@CC --- Make the system available -------------------------------------
@SET-AVAILABLE
@OPERATOR $ *** SYSTEM IS AVAILABLE *** $
@CC ===================================================================
@CC END OF LOAD-MODE:MODE
@CC (the 'system available' MAIL broadcast is done by LOAD-MODE:BATC)
@CC ===================================================================
